# Build context for containers/pool/Dockerfile.
#
# The context is the whole task directory, because the Rust binary resolves
# `defaults/` relative to its compile-time task_dir. That makes exclusions
# load-bearing rather than cosmetic: a local `cargo build` in this checkout
# leaves a ~162 MB `target/` tree that would otherwise ship into the context on
# every build.
#
# Note that `defaults/`, `gold_rust/src`, and `containers/` must NOT be
# excluded — see the Dockerfile header for why.

**/target/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.git/
**/.DS_Store

# Run outputs and captured fixtures: large, and never needed to build.
runs/
**/runs/
data/results/

# The Python gold lane is the authority/debug path and is not used by this
# image; the policy service talks to the Rust engine over HTTP.
gold_python/**/__pycache__/
